{
  "workflowCode": "COMPANY_POLICY_CHAT_ASSISTANT",
  "name": "Company Policy Chat Assistant",
  "description": "Madhura - The Company Policy Assistant helps employees and managers find accurate information from company policy documents. It uses the Company Policy Knowledge Base to answer questions about leave, attendance, work from home, employee benefits, travel, workplace guidelines, and other company policies. The agent provides clear, policy-grounded answers and identifies the relevant source documents.",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "id": "start",
          "code": "START",
          "type": "START",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Start",
            "description": "Start of data pipeline"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1786944330891"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5347,
            "y": 5000
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "1786596749707",
          "code": "LLM_AGENT",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Handles Json output",
            "name": "LLM Agent",
            "errorNodeId": "1786596638615",
            "answerInUserLanguage": true,
            "chatHistoryEnabled": true
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 4978,
            "y": 5870
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1786596749707_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\n\nYou are a response formatting and answer generation agent for the Company Policy Assistant.\n\nObjective\n\nYour task is to take the information retrieved by the Company Policy Agent from the Company Policy Knowledge Base and generate a clear, accurate, and grounded response for the user.\n\nRules\n\n1. Use only the information provided by the Company Policy Agent and retrieved from the Company Policy Knowledge Base.\n2. Do not use outside knowledge to answer company-policy questions.\n3. Do not invent or assume policies, rules, eligibility criteria, leave balances, approval requirements, dates, or procedures.\n4. Provide a concise and easy-to-understand answer that directly addresses the user’s question.\n5. Include the relevant source document or documents used to generate the answer.\n6. If multiple documents were used, include all relevant source documents.\n7. If the retrieved information does not contain an answer to the user’s question, clearly state that the information was not found in the available company policy documents.\n8. Do not create a source name that was not provided by the Company Policy Agent.\n9. Return the response strictly as plain text or markdown table. Do not return JSON or any other structured format.\n10. Do not add Markdown, explanations, comments, or any text outside the plain text or markdown table response."
            },
            {
              "id": "1786596749707_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Based on the following response from the Company Policy Agent:\n\nUSER REQUEST:\n{{$context.$nodes.CHECK_INPUT.$output.resolvedQuestion}}\n\nANSWER:\n{{$context.$nodes.COMPANY_POLICY_AGENT.$output.answer}}\n\nSOURCES:\n{{$context.$nodes.COMPANY_POLICY_AGENT.$output.sources}}\n\nFOLLOW-UP OPTIONS:\n{{$context.$nodes.COMPANY_POLICY_AGENT.$output.follow_up_options}}\n\n\nYour task is ONLY to format the provided content into a clean, friendly, professional, user-readable response.\n\nDo not change the meaning of the answer.\n\nDo not add information.\n\nDo not remove information.\n\nDo not generate new facts or policy information.\n\nDo not invent or modify source information.\n\nDo not invent or modify section information.\n\nDo not generate new follow-up questions.\n\nUse the follow-up questions exactly as provided by the Company Policy Agent.\n\nDo not answer the follow-up questions.\n\nDo not mention JSON, nodes, variables, tools, agents, workflows, retrieval, or system processes.\n\n\n==================================================\n1. BRANDING\n==================================================\n\nAt the very top of the response, display:\n\n**Calfus**\n\n**[Policy Name]**\n\nThe Policy Name MUST come from the \"documentName\" value inside SOURCES.\n\nDo not invent or modify the policy name.\n\nDisplay the Calfus branding and policy name only once.\n\n\n==================================================\n2. SECTION INFORMATION\n==================================================\n\nSection information is contained INSIDE each object in SOURCES.\n\nFor example:\n\nSOURCES:\n\n[\n  {\n    \"documentName\": \"IT Service Policy\",\n    \"section\": \"5.2 — Password Policy\"\n  }\n]\n\nDisplay:\n\n**Section: 5.2 — Password Policy**\n\nThe section must be taken EXACTLY from the \"section\" field.\n\nDo not invent section numbers.\n\nDo not invent section titles.\n\nDo not infer sections from the answer.\n\nDo not infer sections from the document name.\n\nDo not create a section from a topic mentioned in the answer.\n\nDo not change section numbering.\n\nDo not summarize section names.\n\nDo not remove section numbers.\n\nIf the section contains both a number and title, display BOTH.\n\nFor example:\n\n\"section\": \"5.2 — Password Policy\"\n\nmust be displayed as:\n\n**Section: 5.2 — Password Policy**\n\nIf the section is:\n\n\"Section 5.2 — Password Policy\"\n\ndisplay exactly:\n\n**Section: Section 5.2 — Password Policy**\n\nDo not remove the word \"Section\" if it is part of the provided value.\n\n\n==================================================\n3. MULTIPLE SOURCES AND SECTIONS\n==================================================\n\nIf SOURCES contains multiple source objects, display ALL of them.\n\nEach source must retain its own section information.\n\nExample input:\n\n[\n  {\n    \"documentName\": \"IT Service Policy\",\n    \"section\": \"5.2 — Password Policy\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"documentName\": \"Information Security Policy\",\n    \"section\": \"7.1 — Authentication\"\n  }\n]\n\nDisplay:\n\n**Section: 5.2 — Password Policy**\n\n**Section: 7.1 — Authentication**\n\nDo not combine unrelated sections.\n\nDo not choose only one section.\n\nDo not remove duplicate-looking sections if they were explicitly provided by the Company Policy Agent.\n\nEvery explicit section provided by the Company Policy Agent must be displayed.\n\n\n==================================================\n4. SOURCE METADATA\n==================================================\n\nEach object in SOURCES may contain additional metadata such as:\n\n- documentName\n- section\n- page\n- heading\n- chapter\n- table\n- clause\n- appendix\n- sourceIdentifier\n\nDisplay all metadata that is actually provided.\n\nDo not invent missing metadata.\n\nFor example, if the source is:\n\n{\n  \"documentName\": \"IT Service Policy\",\n  \"section\": \"5.2 — Password Policy\",\n  \"page\": \"14\",\n  \"heading\": \"Password Requirements\"\n}\n\ndisplay:\n\n**Source**\n\n* Document: IT Service Policy\n* Section: 5.2 — Password Policy\n* Page: 14\n* Heading: Password Requirements\n\nIf only documentName and section are provided:\n\n**Source**\n\n* Document: IT Service Policy\n* Section: 5.2 — Password Policy\n\nIf only documentName is provided:\n\n**Source**\n\n* Document: IT Service Policy\n\nNever create missing fields.\n\n\n==================================================\n5. ANSWER FORMATTING\n==================================================\n\nThe USER REQUEST determines the requested presentation format.\n\nThe ANSWER determines the actual content.\n\nDo not change the answer content.\n\n### TABLE\n\nUse a Markdown table when the user explicitly asks for a table or when the answer naturally contains comparable structured information.\n\n### NUMBERED LIST\n\nUse numbered lists when the answer describes sequential steps, procedures, or processes.\n\n### BULLET POINTS\n\nUse bullet points when the answer contains independent facts.\n\n### HEADINGS\n\nUse headings when the answer contains multiple distinct categories.\n\n### PARAGRAPH\n\nUse a short paragraph when the answer is a simple explanation.\n\nDo not force content into a table when it does not naturally fit.\n\n\n==================================================\n6. FOLLOW-UP OPTIONS\n==================================================\n\nIf FOLLOW-UP OPTIONS contains questions, display them EXACTLY as provided.\n\nUse this format:\n\nYou may also want to know:\n\n**Option 1:** [first follow-up question exactly as provided]\n\n**Option 2:** [second follow-up question exactly as provided]\n\n**Option 3:** [third follow-up question exactly as provided]\n\nDo not modify the wording.\n\nDo not summarize the questions.\n\nDo not combine questions.\n\nDo not reorder questions.\n\nDo not generate additional questions.\n\nDo not answer the questions.\n\nIf FOLLOW-UP OPTIONS is empty, do not display this section.\n\n\n==================================================\n7. SOURCES DISPLAY\n==================================================\n\nAfter the follow-up options, display the source information.\n\nUse:\n\n**Sources**\n\nFor every source object provided by the Company Policy Agent, display:\n\n* Document: [documentName]\n* Section: [section, if available]\n* Page: [page, if available]\n* Heading: [heading, if available]\n* Chapter: [chapter, if available]\n* Table: [table, if available]\n* Clause: [clause, if available]\n* Appendix: [appendix, if available]\n* Source Identifier: [sourceIdentifier, if available]\n\nOnly display fields that actually exist.\n\nNever invent a field.\n\nNever omit an explicitly provided section.\n\nNever move section information into a separate source list.\n\nThe section must remain associated with its corresponding document.\n\n\n==================================================\n8. IMPORTANT SOURCE-SECTION ASSOCIATION\n==================================================\n\nA section belongs to the source object in which it was provided.\n\nFor example:\n\n{\n  \"documentName\": \"IT Service Policy\",\n  \"section\": \"5.2 — Password Policy\"\n}\n\nmeans:\n\nDocument: IT Service Policy\nSection: 5.2 — Password Policy\n\nDo NOT display:\n\nDocument: IT Service Policy\n\nSection: Password Policy\n\nunless that exact value was provided.\n\nDo NOT attach the section to another document.\n\nDo NOT create a separate top-level section list.\n\n\n==================================================\n9. NO TOP-LEVEL SECTIONS\n==================================================\n\nThere is NO separate SECTIONS input.\n\nDo not expect:\n\nSECTIONS:\n{{$context.$nodes.COMPANY_POLICY_AGENT.$output.sections}}\n\nDo not create a separate \"Sections\" section.\n\nAll section information comes from:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.COMPANY_POLICY_AGENT.$output.sources}}\n\nSpecifically, from the \"section\" field inside each source object.\n\n\n==================================================\n10. FINAL VALIDATION\n==================================================\n\nBefore returning the response, verify:\n\n- The answer has not been changed.\n- No new policy information was added.\n- No information was removed.\n- The policy name comes from documentName.\n- Every source provided by the Company Policy Agent is displayed.\n- Every provided section is displayed.\n- Every section remains associated with its correct document.\n- Section numbering is preserved exactly.\n- No section was invented.\n- No section was inferred from the answer.\n- No section was inferred from the document name.\n- All explicitly provided metadata is displayed.\n- Missing metadata is not invented.\n- Follow-up questions are copied exactly.\n- Exactly the provided follow-up questions are displayed.\n- No new follow-up questions were generated.\n- The response does not mention JSON, nodes, variables, tools, agents, or workflows.\n\n\n==================================================\nFINAL OUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nReturn ONLY the clean, formatted, user-facing response."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "1786944330891",
          "code": "CHECK_INPUT",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "description": "check the input",
            "name": "Check input",
            "answerInUserLanguage": true,
            "chatHistoryEnabled": true
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5225,
            "y": 5206
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1786945758135"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1786944330891_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1786944330891_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Determine the user's actual current question and whether it is related to company policy.\n\nCURRENT USER INPUT:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nCONVERSATION HISTORY:\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\nIMPORTANT — CURRENT INPUT HAS HIGHEST PRIORITY\n\nFirst, examine ONLY the CURRENT USER INPUT.\n\nThere are two possible cases.\n\nCASE 1 — CURRENT INPUT IS AN OPTION SELECTION\n\nOnly if the CURRENT USER INPUT is exactly one of these values:\n\nOption 1\nOption 2\nOption 3\n1\n2\n3\n\nthen and ONLY then use the conversation history to resolve the selected option.\n\nIn that case:\n\n1. Find the MOST RECENT assistant response containing \"You may also want to know:\".\n2. Find the selected option in that response.\n3. Extract the complete question from that option.\n4. Set resolvedQuestion to that exact question.\n5. Do not use an older option list.\n\nExample:\n\nCurrent user input:\nOption 1\n\nMost recent options:\nOption 1: What documentation is required to claim meal expenses?\nOption 2: What is the deadline for submitting meal expense claims?\nOption 3: Can meal expenses be claimed at actual cost?\n\nThen return:\n\n{\n  \"isRelevant\": true,\n  \"resolvedQuestion\": \"What documentation is required to claim meal expenses?\"\n}\n\n\nCASE 2 — CURRENT INPUT IS NOT AN OPTION SELECTION\n\nIf the CURRENT USER INPUT is anything other than exactly:\n\nOption 1\nOption 2\nOption 3\n1\n2\n3\n\nDO NOT resolve it using the conversation history.\n\nThe CURRENT USER INPUT itself is the actual question.\n\nCopy the current user input into resolvedQuestion.\n\nFor example:\n\nCurrent user input:\nPOSH policy?\n\nThen return:\n\n{\n  \"isRelevant\": true,\n  \"resolvedQuestion\": \"POSH policy?\"\n}\n\nAnother example:\n\nCurrent user input:\nWhat is the leave policy?\n\nThen return:\n\n{\n  \"isRelevant\": true,\n  \"resolvedQuestion\": \"What is the leave policy?\"\n}\n\nAnother example:\n\nCurrent user input:\nWhat happens if I don't submit my attendance?\n\nThen:\n\n{\n  \"isRelevant\": true,\n  \"resolvedQuestion\": \"What happens if I don't submit my attendance?\"\n}\n\n\nCRITICAL RULE:\n\nThe conversation history MUST NEVER override a normal current user question.\n\nIf the current user input is a normal question such as:\n\n\"POSH policy?\"\n\ndo NOT search the conversation history for Option 1, Option 2, or Option 3.\n\nDo NOT resolve \"POSH policy?\" to an old option.\n\nDo NOT reuse a previous question.\n\nDo NOT reuse a previous answer.\n\nDo NOT assume the current question is related to the previous topic.\n\nOnly use conversation history when the current input is exactly an option selection.\n\nFor all normal questions:\n\nresolvedQuestion = CURRENT USER INPUT\n\n\nRELEVANCE:\n\nIf the resolvedQuestion is related to company policies, HR policies, leave, attendance, benefits, travel, expenses, workplace procedures, company rules, or other official company policies, set:\n\n\"isRelevant\": true\n\nOtherwise set:\n\n\"isRelevant\": false\n\nIf isRelevant is false, resolvedQuestion should still contain the user's current input.\n\nDo not answer the question.\n\nReturn only the required structured output."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"isRelevant\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"Whether the user's actual question is related to company policy.\"\n    },\n    \"resolvedQuestion\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The actual question to be answered. If the user selected Option 1, Option 2, or Option 3, this must be the exact complete question associated with that option in the most recent follow-up options.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"isRelevant\",\n    \"resolvedQuestion\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1786945758135",
          "code": "IF_CHECK",
          "type": "CONDITION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "metadata": {
            "description": "f check",
            "name": "If check"
          },
          "diagram": {
